it's the world's biggest flying machine  airlander is larger than a Boeing 747  and 24 feet longer than the previous  titleholder the Antonov an-225 this  blimp like airship uses helium to get  off the ground but it uses its  aerodynamic shape to stay in the air it  can hover in the same spot for five days  straight and can land on sand water ice  or snow british aeronautics company  hybrid air vehicles developed the  original model for the u.s. army but the  program ran out of funding in 2013  several months later hybrid air bought  back the airlander project from the  military for 301 thousand dollars the  company plans to sell the massive  airship for 40 million dollars to oil  and mining companies that need to  transport cargo to remote parts of the  world the airlander has attracted some  unusual fans Bruce Dickinson lead singer  of the British heavy metal band Iron  Maiden has invested four hundred and  fifty thousand dollars in the project he  wants to fly it non-stop around the  world and stream the trip over the  Internet  the air Landers maiden voyage is  scheduled for 2016  you
 

